=== QF001 | a builtin used as a parameter
f:{[count] count+1}

=== QF001 | a q keyword from .Q.res, not just the .q namespace
f:{[sin] sin*2}

=== QF001 | qSQL keywords are reserved too
f:{[from] from}

=== clean | a name that merely resembles a builtin is fine
f:{[cnt] cnt+1}

=== clean | `find` and `fill` are operators in q, not names it reserves
f:{[find] find}

=== clean | a builtin name inside a longer name is not the builtin
f:{[counted] counted+1}

=== clean | a builtin as a namespaced field is not a local shadow
.email.subject:"hi"

=== QF002 | the drop operator cannot be a parameter
f:{[_] x+1}

=== QF004 | a definition inside a namespace that shadows a builtin
\d .util
count:{[t] 42}

=== clean | the same name written dotted is not inside the namespace block
.util.count:{[t] 42}

=== QF005 | a nested lambda cannot see the enclosing local
f:{[a] g:{[b] a+b}; g[1]}

=== clean | passing the outer local in explicitly is the fix
f:{[a] g:{[a;b] a+b}; g[a;1]}

=== QF007 | a call in the parameter slot: q refuses the source outright
f:{[tables[]] x+1}

=== QF007 | an expression in the parameter slot
f:{[a+b] 1}

=== QF007 | an integer literal reads as body text, not a parameter
f:{[1] x+1}

=== QF007 | a symbol literal likewise
f:{[`s] x+1}

=== QF007 | two names without a separator is one bracket expression
f:{[a b] a}

=== QF007 | an index in the parameter slot
f:{[a[0]] a}

=== QF007 | an assignment in the parameter slot
f:{[a:1] a}

=== QF007 | a string literal, which the rules see only as blanks
f:{["s"] 1}

=== clean | a dotted name is a legal parameter, surprising as that is
f:{[.q.z] 1}

=== clean | underscores inside a name are fine
f:{[a_b] a_b+1}

=== clean | whitespace around the separators
f:{[ a ; b ] a}

=== QF010 | no space before the body does not hide the global x
f:{[a]x+1}

=== clean | the same shape where the body uses its parameter
f:{[a]a+1}

=== clean | the empty parameter list
f:{[] 42}

=== clean | implicit arguments, with no signature to contradict
f:{x+y}

=== QF008 | a parameter declared twice
f:{[a;a] a}

=== QF008 | and not only adjacently
f:{[a;b;a] a}

=== QF009 | a trailing separator is a third parameter, named `2` by q
f:{[a;b;] a}

=== QF009 | a leading one likewise
f:{[;a] a}

=== QF010 | x is a global here, not an argument: q throws 'x
f:{[a] x+1}

=== QF010 | the same for z
f:{[a] z*2}

=== clean | a global x that does exist is a legitimate reference
x:1;f:{[a] x+1}

=== clean | x declared as the parameter is the argument
f:{[x] x+1}

=== clean | a column named x in qSQL is not the implicit argument
f:{[t] select x from t}

=== QF001 | a join keyword is reserved even though it reads like a name
f:{[aj] aj}

=== QF001 | control words are reserved
f:{[while] while}

=== QF001 | several at once
f:{[count;til] count til}

=== clean | a name q does not reserve, however builtin it sounds
f:{[median] median}
